import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Roadmap — Yaze Media" description="What Kirsten Trimaley is building now through Yaze Media: Archiva and AI News Studio." pageName="Roadmap">
  <section class="roadmap-hero">
    <img src="/images/art/roadmap-river-horizon.webp" srcset="/images/art/roadmap-river-horizon-800.webp 800w, /images/art/roadmap-river-horizon-1600.webp 1600w, /images/art/roadmap-river-horizon.webp 3840w" sizes="100vw" alt="A carved-paper river landscape connecting two current product workshops to a broad horizon" width="3840" height="2160" fetchpriority="high" />
    <div><p class="mono">The work continues</p><h1>My roadmap is a direction,<br /><em>not a promise theatre.</em></h1><p>These are the products I am actively shaping now and the intentions guiding what I build next.</p></div>
  </section>
  <section class="roadmap-intro page-shell"><p class="mono">Current state reviewed 14 September 2026</p><h2>Build carefully. Prove honestly. Keep moving.</h2></section>
  <div class="roadmap-grid page-shell">
    <article><span class="roadmap-state">Now building</span><h2>Archiva</h2><p>A dependable Windows production archive manager for signage work: indexing, preview, search, duplicate review, and carefully planned file movement.</p><h3>Current intention</h3><p>Prove backup, move, and safe-undo behavior against a copied representative archive before the live archive becomes writable.</p><ul><li>Keep the source archive read-only during validation</li><li>Make every planned move inspectable</li><li>Build toward a dependable single-operator V1</li></ul></article>
    <article><span class="roadmap-state">Now building</span><h2>AI News Studio</h2><p>A responsible production path from trusted sources to research packs, claim ledgers, scripts, timed scene plans, and reviewable storyboards.</p><h3>Current intention</h3><p>Complete the visual acquisition, local narration, caption timing, reproducible rendering, and private upload stages before any public-release claim.</p><ul><li>Keep human approval at the publishing boundary</li><li>Track evidence and visual rights with the story</li><li>Turn repeatable editorial work into a clear local workflow</li></ul></article>
  </div>
  <section class="roadmap-signature page-shell"><img src="/images/brand/yazekt-avatar.jpg" alt="YazeKT brand avatar" width="1254" height="1254" /><div><p class="mono">Kirsten Trimaley / Yaze Media</p><h2>I’m building a practice that lasts.</h2><p>The next chapter is not about chasing every new tool. It is about using strong visual judgment, AI-assisted development, and increasingly rigorous verification to make useful products.</p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
